  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev16-08",
    "question": "<p>(a) Using the formulae for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r\"></span> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^{2}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r^{3}\"></span> , show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} r(r+1)(r+3)=\\frac{1}{12} n(n+1)(n+2)(3 n+k),\"></span> where k is a constant to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></p><p>(b) Hence evaluate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=21}^{40} r(r+1)(r+3).\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>The expanded summand is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r^3+4r^2+3r\"></span>; collect the three standard sums over denominator <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\"></span>. A check on the unknown is available at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\"></span>: the single product is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8\"></span>, while the proposed expression is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3+k)/2\"></span>, forcing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=13\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_j=\\sum_{r=1}^n r^j\"></span>. Expanding the summand gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=3 T_{1} + 4 T_{2} + T_{3}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Substitute <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_3=\\frac{n^{2} \\left(n + 1\\right)^{2}}{4}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=\\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right) \\left(2 n + 1\\right)}{6}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1=\\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right)}{2}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[4]</small></p>",
      "<p>Consequently <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=\\frac{n^{2} \\left(n + 1\\right)^{2}}{4} + \\frac{2 n \\left(n + 1\\right) \\left(2 n + 1\\right)}{3} + \\frac{3 n \\left(n + 1\\right)}{2}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Simplifying and factorising gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=\\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right) \\left(n + 2\\right) \\left(3 n + 13\\right)}{12}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=13\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(b) Subtract the partial sums <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_{40}-S_{20}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>This gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(763420\\right)-\\left(56210\\right)=707210\"></span>.  <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 9 marks.</p>",
