  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev16-09",
    "question": "<p>(a) Show, using the formulae for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum r\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum r^{2}\"></span> , that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\left( 6 r^{2}+4 r-1 \\right)=n \\left( n+2 \\right)\\left( 2 n+1 \\right)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>(b) Hence, or otherwise, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=11}^{20} \\left( 6 r^{2}+4 r-1 \\right).\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Separate the quadratic, linear and constant contributions. Summing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6r^2+4r-1\"></span> gives a term <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-n\"></span>, rather than a single subtraction of one. In the numerical interval subtract through 10 to keep the ten terms starting at 11.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_j=\\sum_{r=1}^n r^j\"></span>. Expanding the summand gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=- T_{0} + 4 T_{1} + 6 T_{2}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Substitute <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=\\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right) \\left(2 n + 1\\right)}{6}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1=\\frac{n \\left(n + 1\\right)}{2}\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_0=n\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Consequently <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=n \\left(n + 1\\right) \\left(2 n + 1\\right) + 2 n \\left(n + 1\\right) - n\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Simplifying and factorising gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_n=n \\left(n + 2\\right) \\left(2 n + 1\\right)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) Subtract the partial sums <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_{20}-S_{10}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>This gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(18040\\right)-\\left(2520\\right)=15520\"></span>.  <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
